# .bpmignore — gitignore-syntax denylist applied to the tarball-relative
# paths during `bpm publish`.
#
# What's already in the tarball before this filter runs:
#   - The plugin binary, renamed to the canonical filename at the root
#   - Everything under build/<triple>/ flattened to the tarball root
#   - README* / LICENSE* / NOTICES* at the root
#   - The `main` file + its directory (e.g. lib/index.bnl + lib/*) at
#     their project-relative paths
#
# This file scrubs the CMake / MSBuild noise that the binDir flatten
# would otherwise drag in. Patterns are gitignore-style and are matched
# against the path the file will have *inside the tarball*.

# Anything bpm download writes that we don't want re-shipped.
deps

# CMake / MSBuild build artefacts (all relative to tarball root, since
# build/<triple>/ is flattened to root).
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.vcxproj
*.vcxproj.filters
*.slnx
*.dir/
ALL_BUILD*
ZERO_CHECK*

# MSBuild intermediate / output dirs that end up flattened too.
Release/
Debug/
x64/
x86/

# Machine-specific IDE leftovers in case any sneak in.
.vscode/
.idea/
CMakeUserPresets.json
